<rml>
<head>
    <title>Moments</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="scrim">
        <div class="case">

            <div class="lid stacked">
                <div class="lid-top">
                    <div class="head">
                        <div class="mark"></div>
                        <div class="title">Moments</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chrome">
                        <div class="win-btn" id="modal-close"><svg class="win-ic" src="../icons/x.svg"/></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hint">Up and down to choose, Enter takes you to the buttons, left and right between them, Escape or the pad's B goes back</div>
            </div>

            <!-- Nine slots: the autosave's, then eight of the player's. Built by the shell from the
                 slot files at the moment the screen opens (phase 77, .scaffold/states/): a thumbnail
                 where one exists, the name, the scene and the time. An empty slot says so and offers
                 itself. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="moment-rows"></div>

            <!-- Save here writes the focused slot (in play only; the launcher offers Resume alone),
                 Resume loads it, Delete removes it, Mark as reserved moves it where nothing writes
                 over it (and Unreserve back). Nothing here is one click from losing progress:
                 Delete asks twice, the same way Uninstall does. Two to a row (case.rcss,
                 .pairs), so none of them is crushed in the panel; Cancel alone across the foot. -->
            <div class="actions pairs">
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="moments-delete"><span class="act-label" id="moments-delete-label">Delete</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="moments-reserve"><span class="act-label" id="moments-reserve-label">Mark as reserved</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="moments-save"><span class="act-label" id="moments-save-label">Save here</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-play" id="moments-load"><span class="act-label" id="moments-load-label">Load</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn" id="moments-cancel"><span class="act-label">Cancel</span></div>
            </div>

            <!-- THE ONE LINE OF HONESTY, always shown (states-design.md section 8). -->
            <div class="foot">
                <span id="moments-note">A moment keeps your progress and where you stand. Enemies, platforms and effects start over, as when the game loads a file. Rewind is not offered: the program cannot freeze the game mid frame.</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
<rml>
<head>
    <title>Photo mode guide</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="medallion.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="prompts.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- PHOTO MODE'S BUTTON GUIDE (the user, 2026-10-13): what each control does while photo mode holds
     the game, drawn as the menu's footer draws its prompts, on the device in use and as it is
     bound (ui/prompts/photo_guide.h). The shell shows it while photo mode holds the game, no menu
     is open and its binding has not hidden it. The list is the shell model's `guide`, a fixed
     length with the unused slots empty and hidden, as the footer's is. -->
<body class="overlay" data-model="shell">
    <div class="pg">
        <div class="pg-band" id="pg-band">
            <div class="pr" data-for="p : guide" data-attr-id="'guide-' + p.action"
                 data-class-pr-empty="p.kind == ''"
                 data-class-t-xa="p.tint == 'xbox-a'" data-class-t-xb="p.tint == 'xbox-b'"
                 data-class-t-xx="p.tint == 'xbox-x'" data-class-t-xy="p.tint == 'xbox-y'"
                 data-class-t-pc="p.tint == 'ps-cross'" data-class-t-po="p.tint == 'ps-circle'"
                 data-class-t-ps="p.tint == 'ps-square'" data-class-t-pt="p.tint == 'ps-triangle'">
                <div class="md pr-md" data-if="p.kind == 'face' || p.kind == 'medal'">
                    <div class="ly shadows"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-l-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-r-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly rim"></div>
                    <svg class="pr-shape" data-if="p.shape != ''" data-class-pr-drawn="p.kind == 'medal'" data-attr-src="'prompts/' + p.shape + '.svg'"/>
                    <span class="pr-letter" data-if="p.shape == ''"><span>{{p.key}}</span></span>
                </div>
                <div class="pr-plate" data-if="p.kind == 'plate'"><span class="pl-l"></span><span class="pl-m"><span class="pr-word">{{p.key}}</span></span><span class="pl-r"></span></div>
                <div class="pr-pad" data-if="p.kind == 'pad'"></div>
                <svg class="pr-art" data-if="p.kind == 'art'" data-attr-src="'prompts/' + p.shape + '.svg'"/>
                <span class="pr-label" data-if="p.label != ''">{{p.label}}</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
/* THE PROMPTS: a button of the device in use and what it does (the menus plan, phase 109). Drawn
 * by the menu's footer (shell.rml, inside .sh-prompts) and by photo mode's button guide
 * (photo-guide.rml, inside .pg), so both read from these rules and look the same. Their sizes are
 * the footer's own tokens, held at their 100% size below 100% (tokens.rcss, .prompts-full-size).
 */

.pr
{
	display: flex;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	align-items: center;
	margin-right: var(--pr-gap);
}

/* An unused slot of the footer (it keeps a fixed length, shell_model.h). */
.pr.pr-empty
{
	display: none;
}

.pr:hover .pr-label
{
	color: var(--color-ink);
}

.pr .pr-md
{
	width: var(--md-prompt-size);
	height: var(--md-prompt-height);
}

.pr-shape
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	image-color: var(--color-ink);
}

/* THE D-PAD AND THE STICKS (the pad prompts canvas, approved 2026-10-13): drawn in the medallion
 * like a face button's shape, but in their own colors (lit arms and chevrons in ink, the rest dim),
 * so the shape is left untinted. */
.pr-shape.pr-drawn
{
	image-color: var(--color-untinted);
}

/* A SMALL SYSTEM BUTTON (Options, Share, Create, View, Menu, Mute, Home and the rest; the same
 * canvas): one drawing, the button's shape over the left end of a stone carrying its word, on the
 * plates' 190 high box, so it stands at the plates' height and its width follows the drawing. */
.pr-art
{
	flex: 0 0 auto;
	height: var(--plate-pr-height);
}

/* A letter on a face button, centered on the disc (90 of the medallion's 190, a little above the
 * box's middle, hence the lift). Centered by the box, never by a share of the width: a percentage
 * padding is a share of the WIDTH in RCSS, which is what pushed the plates' words off center. */
.pr-letter
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	padding-bottom: var(--plate-text-lift);
	font-family: var(--font-mono);
	font-weight: var(--weight-mono-strong);
	font-size: var(--size-prompt);
	color: var(--color-ink);
}

/* A word on its plate, centered on the plate's rounded rectangle, which is a little above the
 * drawing's middle (the drawing also holds the ground shadow under it): 90 of its 190, so the
 * word is lifted by half the padding. (The user, 2026-10-13: "make sure text in the rectangular
 * button are properly centered in them".) */
.pr-pad
{
	width: var(--pad-pr-width);
	height: var(--plate-pr-height);
	decorator: svg(prompts/touchpad.svg);
	margin-right: var(--plate-pr-overlap);
}

/* THE PLATE WIDENS WITH ITS WORD (the user, 2026-10-13: "for like things like enter or you know
 * other longer words, they need to actually expand and get a little bit wider ... especially for like
 * options, which ... overlaps the edges"). Its two ends, with the leaves, keep their width; the
 * straight middle between them is at least as wide again and grows with the word, so a short word
 * draws the plate exactly as before and a long one a longer plate (tools/brand_art.mjs cuts the
 * drawing). The word reaches a little into each end, where the rounded rectangle still runs flat. */
.pr-plate
{
	display: flex;
	height: var(--plate-pr-height);
	margin-right: var(--plate-pr-overlap);
}

.pr-plate .pl-l,
.pr-plate .pl-r
{
	flex: 0 0 var(--plate-cap-width);
	width: var(--plate-cap-width);
}

.pr-plate .pl-l { decorator: svg(prompts/plate-left.svg); }
.pr-plate .pl-r { decorator: svg(prompts/plate-right.svg); }

/* The middle and its word paint above both ends: the word reaches into them, and the right end,
   drawn after it, would otherwise cover its last letter ("Ente" for Enter). It also runs a pixel
   under each end (--plate-seam), the same flat band their inner edges carry, so the pieces can
   never round apart into a seam. */
.pr-plate .pl-m
{
	position: relative;
	z-index: var(--layer-plate-word);
	flex: 1 0 auto;
	margin-left: var(--plate-seam);
	margin-right: var(--plate-seam);
	min-width: var(--plate-cap-width);
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	padding-bottom: var(--plate-text-lift);
	decorator: svg(prompts/plate-mid.svg);
}

.pr-plate .pr-word
{
	margin: 0 var(--plate-word-reach);
	white-space: nowrap;
}

.pr-word
{
	line-height: 1;
	font-family: var(--font-mono);
	font-weight: var(--weight-mono-strong);
	font-size: var(--pr-word-size);
	color: var(--color-ink);
}

.pr-label
{
	margin-left: var(--pr-label-gap);
	white-space: nowrap;
}

/* The face buttons' pastels, as each family's controllers code them. */
.t-xa .pr-letter { color: var(--color-xbox-a); }
.t-xb .pr-letter { color: var(--color-xbox-b); }
.t-xx .pr-letter { color: var(--color-xbox-x); }
.t-xy .pr-letter { color: var(--color-xbox-y); }
.t-pc .pr-shape { image-color: var(--color-ps-cross); }
.t-po .pr-shape { image-color: var(--color-ps-circle); }
.t-ps .pr-shape { image-color: var(--color-ps-square); }
.t-pt .pr-shape { image-color: var(--color-ps-triangle); }

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * PHOTO MODE'S BUTTON GUIDE (the user, 2026-10-13: "a row of buttons ... the small buttons kind of
 * like in the footer of the launcher ... at the bottom of the screen when enabling the photo
 * mode"): the footer's prompts on a band of the footer's ground, centered at the bottom of the
 * picture, over the frozen game. It takes no clicks (body.overlay); its binding hides it.
 */
.pg
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: var(--pg-bottom);
	display: flex;
	justify-content: center;
}

.pg-band
{
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	min-height: var(--prompts-height);
	/* Each prompt keeps its gap after it, so the band's left padding is that gap: even both sides. */
	padding: 0 0 0 var(--pr-gap);
	background-color: var(--color-scrim);
	border-top: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
	font-size: var(--pr-text);
	color: var(--color-dim);
}

