<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="200" height="190" viewBox="0 0 200 190"><!-- A face button's triangle, white, for the stylesheet to tint. Generated by tools/brand_art.mjs; do not edit. --><path d="M100 64 L124 106 L76 106Z" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="8" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"/></svg>
<rml>
<head>
    <title>Recorder</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
</head>
<body class="overlay">
    <!-- The frame recorder's plate (the user's ask of 2026-09-22): "an overlay element that sits
         it top left just like the fps does in top right". The same plate as the frame rate
         counter, in the opposite corner. Unlike the counter it does NOT move when the title bar
         appears; case.rcss says why, and the short version is that a button which slides out from
         under the pointer aiming at it is not a button.

         THE WHOLE PLATE IS THE BUTTON. One click starts a recording of the length the settings
         row holds, and one more ends it early. The dot is what says which of those a click will
         do, so the state is readable at a glance from across the room rather than needing the
         words to be read. -->
    <div class="counter recorder" id="recorder">
        <div class="mark"></div>
        <span class="counter-value" id="record-text">Record</span>
        <!-- THE DOT IS A DIVIDER AS WELL AS A STATE (the user's ask of 2026-09-23). It sat
             between the mark and the word, where it read as a second mark and left `Record` and
             `0:05` touching each other with nothing between them. Between the two it separates
             them and still carries the color that says whether a click starts or stops. -->
        <span class="dot" id="record-dot"></span>
        <span class="counter-unit" id="record-note"></span>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
<rml>
<head>
    <title>Settings</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="scrim" id="settings-scrim">
        <div class="case">

            <div class="lid stacked">
                <div class="lid-top">
                    <div class="head">
                        <div class="mark"></div>
                        <div class="title">Settings</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chrome">
                        <div class="win-btn" id="modal-close"><svg class="win-ic" src="../icons/x.svg"/></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hint">Up and down to move, left and right to change, Escape or the pad's B closes</div>
            </div>

            <!-- THE ROWS ARE BUILT FROM THE MODEL, NOT LISTED HERE, exactly as the controls
                 document and the debug menu build theirs. This used to be a fixed run of row
                 elements, and on 2026-09-22 adding two settings pushed three rows off the end of
                 it: a row with no element simply does not appear, so Controls, Your files and
                 Debug vanished while the menu looked perfectly normal. Slots were added, and then
                 the user asked the better question ("but can we not just add scrollable areas?"),
                 which is this. There is now no number here to get wrong, and a list longer than
                 the case scrolls instead of being cut off. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="settings-rows" data-model="rows"></div>

            <!-- Quit is an ACTION, drawn in the same bar the launcher uses, alone: there is
                 nothing to Play from inside the game. It was missing here altogether once the two
                 buttons left the list (the user, 2026-09-23), and with the title bar off this
                 menu is the only way out of the program. It keeps its place at the end of the
                 keyboard and pad order. -->
            <div class="actions">
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="act-quit"><span class="act-label" id="act-quit-label">Quit</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="foot">
                <span>Saved as you change it</span>
                <span id="settings-foot">F1 closes this, F2 is about, F3 is controls</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
/* THE SHELL (the menus plan, phase 96): what is drawn around the page, in four placements, from
 * the design decision (.scaffold/menus/design/decision/, C Medallion, with its ADDENDUM):
 *
 *   launcher  the launcher's own window: the head, the dial, the page, the prompts, full width
 *   left      the panel docked against the left edge, its right edge cut on a slant into the
 *             picture with the gold lit line (cut.rcss)
 *   right     the same panel mirrored against the right edge
 *   center    the Ledger with medallions: a rail of every section down the left of a centered
 *             panel over a scrim, the page beside it
 *
 * Tokens only (tools/check_tokens.py). Positions inside the dial are shares of its box, so the
 * dial keeps its shape at every interface size. */

/* THE FRAME STAYS BEHIND ITS PAGE (2026-10-22; the user: "when clicking certain places in menu with
 * cursor like the highlighted area in screenshot, it hides all settings"). The page is its own
 * document laid into #sh-host, and the shell is pushed behind it whenever it is refreshed
 * (ui_shell.cpp, refresh_shell). A click on the frame's empty space (the head, the dial between its
 * medallions) refreshes nothing, but RmlUi raised the shell to the front anyway because it took the
 * focus, and its ground covered the page until the next refresh. An explicit z-index is never raised. */
body.shell
{
	z-index: var(--layer-document);
	font-family: var(--font-body);
	font-weight: var(--weight-body);
	font-size: var(--size-row);
	color: var(--color-ink);
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
}

.sh-scrim
{
	display: none;
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	background-color: var(--color-scrim-full);
}

.center .sh-scrim
{
	display: block;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The panel and its ground
 */

/* BORDER-BOX (the user, 2026-10-13: "the right border falls off ... as if the left border pushes it
 * one pixel too far right"): the launcher's panel is the window's full width with an edge each
 * side, and a width that left its edges out put the right one past the window. */
.sh-panel
{
	position: absolute;
	top: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	left: 0;
	width: var(--panel-width);
	box-sizing: border-box;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
}

.launcher .sh-panel
{
	width: 100%;
	border: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
}

.right .sh-panel
{
	left: auto;
	right: 0;
}

.center .sh-panel
{
	top: 7%;
	bottom: 7%;
	left: 9%;
	width: 82%;
	max-width: var(--ledger-width);
	display: block;
	border: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
}

/* The ground stops where the cut begins, so the slant is the panel's own edge. */
.sh-ground
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	right: var(--cut-edge-width);
	background-color: var(--color-slate);
	overflow: hidden;
}

.right .sh-ground
{
	right: 0;
	left: var(--cut-edge-width);
}

.launcher .sh-ground,
.center .sh-ground
{
	right: 0;
}

.sh-cut,
.sh-cut-mirror
{
	display: none;
}

.left .sh-cut,
.right .sh-cut-mirror
{
	display: block;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The head and the logo
 */

.sh-mast
{
	position: relative;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	height: var(--mast-height-docked);
	margin-right: var(--cut-edge-width);
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	/* Docked, the logo is centered (2026-10-13); the launcher and the rail keep it at the left. */
	justify-content: center;
	background-color: var(--color-slate-deep);
	border-bottom: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
}

.right .sh-mast
{
	margin-right: 0;
	margin-left: var(--cut-edge-width);
}

.launcher .sh-mast
{
	height: var(--mast-height);
	margin-right: 0;
	justify-content: space-between;
	padding-left: var(--space-6);
	align-items: stretch;
}

.center .sh-mast
{
	justify-content: space-between;
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: var(--rail-width);
	height: var(--mast-height);
	margin: 0;
	padding-left: var(--space-4);
	border-right: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
}

.logo
{
	position: relative;
	width: var(--logo-width-docked);
	height: var(--logo-height-docked);
}

.launcher .logo
{
	width: var(--logo-width);
	height: var(--logo-height);
	margin-top: auto;
	margin-bottom: auto;
}

.center .logo
{
	width: var(--logo-width-rail);
	height: var(--logo-height-rail);
}

.logo-slab
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	decorator: svg(brand/logo.svg);
}

/* The medallion over the slab's left end, in the lockup's own proportions: its 290 by 276 box
 * at (30, 170) against the logo's crop of 896 by 237 at (55, 200). */
.logo .logo-md
{
	position: absolute;
	left: -2.79%;
	top: -12.66%;
	width: 32.37%;
	height: 116.46%;
}

/* The mark in the disc, raised to sit optically centered (the user, 2026-10-12), in the
 * medallion's 200 by 190 canvas: 64 by 53.3 at (68, 57.4). */
.logo .logo-mark
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 34%;
	top: 30.21%;
	width: 32%;
	height: 28.05%;
}

.sh-side
{
	display: none;
}

.launcher .sh-side
{
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: space-between;
	align-items: flex-end;
}

.sh-win
{
	display: flex;
}

.sh-wb
{
	width: var(--window-btn-width);
	height: var(--window-btn-height);
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	transition: background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease);
}

.sh-wb:hover
{
	background-color: var(--color-slate-raised);
}

.sh-wb:hover .win-ic
{
	image-color: var(--color-ink);
}

.sh-close:hover
{
	background-color: var(--color-error);
}

.sh-close:hover .win-ic
{
	image-color: var(--color-on-lime);
}

.sh-ver
{
	font-family: var(--font-mono);
	font-size: var(--size-label);
	color: var(--color-faint);
	padding: 0 var(--space-5) var(--space-4) 0;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The dial
 */

.sh-dial
{
	position: relative;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	height: var(--shell-dial-height-docked);
	margin-right: var(--cut-edge-width);
	background-color: var(--color-slate-deep);
	border-bottom: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
}

.right .sh-dial
{
	margin-right: 0;
	margin-left: var(--cut-edge-width);
}

.launcher .sh-dial
{
	height: var(--shell-dial-height);
	margin-right: 0;
}

.sec
{
	position: absolute;
	transform: translateX(-50%);
	transition: left var(--duration-base) var(--ease), top var(--duration-base) var(--ease);
}

.sec .md
{
	width: var(--md-dial-size);
	height: var(--md-dial-height);
}

.sec.cur .md
{
	width: var(--md-current-size);
	height: var(--md-current-height);
}

.sec:hover .md
{
	transform: translateY(-4%);
}

.sec-name
{
	display: none;
}

/* A SHALLOW ARC (the user, 2026-10-13: "don't offset the vertical positioning quite so much between the
 * main selection and the outer two selections ... don't drop them as much. That would also reduce some
 * of that space"): each step out from the current one drops less, so the dial needs less height. */
.sec.slot-l2 { left: 12%; top: 32%; }
.sec.slot-l1 { left: 31%; top: 16%; }
.sec.slot-c  { left: 50%; top: 3%; }
.sec.slot-r1 { left: 69%; top: 16%; }
.sec.slot-r2 { left: 88%; top: 32%; }
.sec.slot-off { display: none; }

.launcher .sec.slot-l2 { left: 21%; top: 30%; }
.launcher .sec.slot-l1 { left: 34%; top: 15%; }
.launcher .sec.slot-r1 { left: 66%; top: 15%; }
.launcher .sec.slot-r2 { left: 79%; top: 30%; }

/* THE BUTTONS THAT TURN THE DIAL, AT ITS TOP CORNERS (the user, 2026-10-22: "pinned to like the top
 * left and the top right in that little space so that the user can accurately see that those are the
 * buttons that are used to move those specific areas"). The arc leaves the corners above its outer
 * medallions empty; the plates stand there, clear of them. The footer's plates overlap their
 * neighbor (--plate-pr-overlap); these stand alone, so neither carries that margin. */
.sh-pin
{
	position: absolute;
	top: var(--space-2);
	margin-right: 0;
}

.sh-pin .pr-plate
{
	margin-right: 0;
}

.sh-pin-l
{
	left: var(--space-4);
}

.sh-pin-r
{
	right: var(--space-4);
}

/* The current section's name, on a plate that hangs over the dial's lower line into the page. */
.sh-name
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	bottom: var(--name-drop-below);
	transform: translateX(-50%);
	padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-4);
	font-family: var(--font-display);
	font-weight: var(--weight-display-max);
	font-size: var(--size-display);
	text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--color-ink);
	background-color: var(--color-slate-deep);
	border: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
	white-space: nowrap;
}

/* The rail (centered): every section down the left, each a small medallion with its name; the
 * current one lit. The dial's slots mean nothing here. */
.center .sh-dial
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: var(--mast-height);
	bottom: 0;
	width: var(--rail-width);
	height: auto;
	margin: 0;
	padding-top: var(--space-4);
	border-bottom: 0;
	border-right: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
}

.center .sec,
.center .sec.slot-l2, .center .sec.slot-l1, .center .sec.slot-c,
.center .sec.slot-r1, .center .sec.slot-r2, .center .sec.slot-off
{
	position: relative;
	left: auto;
	top: auto;
	transform: none;
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	height: var(--rail-item-height);
	padding: 0 var(--space-4);
}

.center .sec .md,
.center .sec.cur .md
{
	width: var(--md-row-size);
	height: var(--md-row-height);
}

.center .sec-name
{
	display: block;
	margin-left: var(--space-3);
	font-family: var(--font-display);
	font-weight: var(--weight-display);
	font-size: var(--size-heading);
	text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--color-dim);
}

.center .sec.cur
{
	background-color: var(--color-plate-on);
	border-left: var(--edge-focus) var(--color-lime);
}

.center .sec.cur .sec-name
{
	color: var(--color-ink);
}

.center .sh-name
{
	left: auto;
	right: auto;
	bottom: auto;
	transform: none;
	display: none;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The page's box: the section's own document is laid into it.
 */

.sh-host
{
	flex: 1 1 auto;
	margin: var(--host-top) var(--host-side-cut) var(--host-bottom) var(--host-side-docked);
}

.right .sh-host
{
	margin-left: var(--host-side-cut);
	margin-right: var(--host-side-docked);
}

.launcher .sh-host
{
	margin-left: var(--host-side);
	margin-right: var(--host-side);
}

.center .sh-host
{
	position: absolute;
	left: var(--rail-width);
	right: 0;
	top: 0;
	bottom: var(--prompts-height);
	margin: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The prompts
 */

/* Positioned, like the head and the dial, so it paints over the panel's ground. */
.sh-prompts
{
	position: relative;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	/* A narrow panel takes a second line rather than pressing the prompts into each other. */
	min-height: var(--prompts-height);
	margin-right: var(--cut-edge-width);
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	align-items: center;
	align-content: center;
	padding: 0 var(--space-6) 0 var(--host-side-docked);
	background-color: var(--color-slate-deep);
	border-top: var(--rule) var(--color-line);
	font-size: var(--pr-text);
	color: var(--color-dim);
}

.right .sh-prompts
{
	margin-right: 0;
	margin-left: var(--cut-edge-width);
	padding-left: var(--space-8);
}

.launcher .sh-prompts
{
	margin-right: 0;
	padding-left: var(--space-6);
}

.center .sh-prompts
{
	position: absolute;
	left: var(--rail-width);
	right: 0;
	bottom: 0;
	margin: 0;
	padding-left: var(--space-8);
}

/* The prompts themselves, a button and what it does, are prompts.rcss: the button guide in photo
 * mode draws them too (photo-guide.rml). */

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The paused badge, over the picture's far corner while the game is paused: the dial's own
 * medallion at its own size, its rim gold and still (nothing to press, so never lime), a pause
 * glyph in its face, and the word on a plate of the deep slate under it so it reads over any scene.
 */

.sh-held
{
	position: absolute;
	right: var(--held-margin);
	bottom: var(--held-margin);
	width: var(--held-size);
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	align-items: center;
}

.sh-held .held-md
{
	--md-size: var(--held-size);
	--md-height: var(--held-md-height);
}

.held-word
{
	margin-top: var(--space-1);
	padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
	background-color: var(--color-slate-deep);
	font-family: var(--font-mono);
	font-weight: var(--weight-mono-strong);
	font-size: var(--size-label-sm);
	letter-spacing: var(--tracking-badge);
	text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--color-ink);
}

.right .sh-held
{
	right: auto;
	left: var(--held-margin);
}

/* Centered, the panel takes the middle of the picture; the badge goes to its top corner. */
.center .sh-held
{
	top: var(--space-4);
	bottom: auto;
	right: var(--space-4);
}
<rml>
<head>
    <title>Menu</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="medallion.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="cut.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="shell.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="prompts.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- THE ONE MENU (the menus plan, phase 96): the launcher before Play and the in-game menu after
     it are this document. It draws what is around the page: the head with the logo, the dial of
     section medallions, the current section's name, the prompts, the held badge. The page itself
     is the section's own document, laid into the box #sh-host leaves for it (src/ui/ui_shell.cpp,
     place_page), until each section moves in. The data model "shell" (src/ui/models/
     shell_model.h) carries the router's answer; the placement is a class on the body.

     The dial and the prompts are for the pointer and the shoulders only: data-nav="pointer"
     keeps them out of the directions, which move within the page (nav_rml.h). -->
<body class="shell" data-model="shell"
      data-class-launcher="placement == 'launcher'" data-class-left="placement == 'left'"
      data-class-right="placement == 'right'" data-class-center="placement == 'center'">

    <div class="sh-scrim"></div>

    <div class="sh-panel" id="sh-panel">
        <div class="sh-ground"><div class="survey"></div></div>
        <div class="cut-edge sh-cut"></div>
        <div class="cut-edge mirror sh-cut-mirror"></div>

        <!-- The head: the logo, and in the launcher's own window its buttons and the version. The
             band is the window's drag area (main/launch.cpp), its buttons excepted. -->
        <div class="sh-mast" id="sh-mast">
            <div class="logo">
                <div class="logo-slab"></div>
                <div class="md logo-md">
                    <div class="ly shadows"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-l-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-r-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly rim"></div>
                    <div class="mark logo-mark"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sh-side">
                <div class="sh-win">
                    <div class="sh-wb" id="win-min" data-nav="pointer"><svg class="win-ic" src="../icons/minus.svg"/></div>
                    <div class="sh-wb" id="win-max" data-nav="pointer"><svg class="win-ic" src="../icons/square.svg"/></div>
                    <div class="sh-wb sh-close" id="win-close" data-nav="pointer"><svg class="win-ic" src="../icons/x.svg"/></div>
                </div>
                <span class="sh-ver">{{version}}</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The dial: every section as a medallion; the current one large and lit, two either side,
             the rest off the dial until it turns. In the centered placement it is the rail, every
             section listed with its name. -->
        <div class="sh-dial" id="sh-dial">
            <div class="sec" data-for="s : sections" data-nav="pointer" data-attr-id="'sec-' + s.id"
                 data-class-slot-l2="s.slot == -2" data-class-slot-l1="s.slot == -1" data-class-slot-c="s.slot == 0"
                 data-class-slot-r1="s.slot == 1" data-class-slot-r2="s.slot == 2" data-class-slot-off="s.slot == 99"
                 data-class-cur="s.current">
                <div class="md" data-class-is-f="s.current">
                    <div class="ly shadows"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-l-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-r-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly rim"></div>
                    <div class="ly glint"></div>
                    <svg class="glyph" data-attr-src="'../icons/' + s.glyph + '.svg'"/>
                </div>
                <span class="sec-name">{{s.name}}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sh-name" id="sh-name">{{title}}</div>
            <!-- The buttons that turn the dial, pinned at its top corners, back at the left and on at
                 the right (the user, 2026-10-22: "above the little rotating medallions. That way
                 they're more visible"). Each a plate on every device (src/ui/prompts, dial_pair), a
                 click for the mouse like any prompt; empty, and so hidden, on the rail and while
                 the on-screen keyboard is up, when the footer carries them. -->
            <div class="pr sh-pin" data-for="p : pins" data-nav="pointer" data-attr-id="'prompt-' + p.action"
                 data-class-pr-empty="p.kind == ''"
                 data-class-sh-pin-l="p.action == 'dial-prev'" data-class-sh-pin-r="p.action == 'dial-next'">
                <div class="pr-plate"><span class="pl-l"></span><span class="pl-m"><span class="pr-word">{{p.key}}</span></span><span class="pl-r"></span></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The page's box. Nothing is drawn here: the section's document is laid into it. -->
        <div class="sh-host" id="sh-host"></div>

        <!-- The prompts: what the device in use does here, each a click for the mouse. -->
        <div class="sh-prompts" id="sh-prompts">
            <div class="pr" data-for="p : prompts" data-nav="pointer" data-attr-id="'prompt-' + p.action"
                 data-class-pr-empty="p.kind == ''"
                 data-class-t-xa="p.tint == 'xbox-a'" data-class-t-xb="p.tint == 'xbox-b'"
                 data-class-t-xx="p.tint == 'xbox-x'" data-class-t-xy="p.tint == 'xbox-y'"
                 data-class-t-pc="p.tint == 'ps-cross'" data-class-t-po="p.tint == 'ps-circle'"
                 data-class-t-ps="p.tint == 'ps-square'" data-class-t-pt="p.tint == 'ps-triangle'">
                <div class="md pr-md" data-if="p.kind == 'face' || p.kind == 'medal'">
                    <div class="ly shadows"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-l-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly leaf-r-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-c"></div>
                    <div class="ly rim"></div>
                    <svg class="pr-shape" data-if="p.shape != ''" data-class-pr-drawn="p.kind == 'medal'" data-attr-src="'prompts/' + p.shape + '.svg'"/>
                    <span class="pr-letter" data-if="p.shape == ''"><span>{{p.key}}</span></span>
                </div>
                <div class="pr-plate" data-if="p.kind == 'plate'"><span class="pl-l"></span><span class="pl-m"><span class="pr-word">{{p.key}}</span></span><span class="pl-r"></span></div>
                <div class="pr-pad" data-if="p.kind == 'pad'"></div>
                <svg class="pr-art" data-if="p.kind == 'art'" data-attr-src="'prompts/' + p.shape + '.svg'"/>
                <span class="pr-label" data-if="p.label != ''">{{p.label}}</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The game is paused while the menu is open (phase 97). The real medallion, the dial's own
         layers, with a pause glyph in its face and the word under it (the user, 2026-10-13: "change
         held to Paused and use the real medallion graphic"). -->
    <div class="sh-held" data-if="held">
        <div class="md held-md">
            <div class="ly shadows"></div>
            <div class="ly leaf-l-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-c"></div>
            <div class="ly leaf-r-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-c"></div>
            <div class="ly rim"></div>
            <svg class="glyph" src="../icons/pause.svg"/>
        </div>
        <span class="held-word">Paused</span>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
/* THE SPLASH (the menus plan, phase 99), option D of design-canvas://96729e1b, laid out in the
 * launcher's own 960 by 620 window from the decision's numbers (tokens.rcss). Tokens only. */

body.splash
{
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	display: flex;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
	font-family: var(--font-body);
	color: var(--color-dim);
	decorator: radial-gradient(circle at 38% 46%, var(--splash-light) 0%, var(--color-slate) 50%, var(--splash-dark) 100%);
	opacity: 1;
	transition: opacity var(--splash-fade) var(--ease);
	overflow: hidden;
}

/* The launcher's own size, centered in whatever the window is: it opens maximized (the user,
 * 2026-10-13), and every part below is placed within this stage as the decision drew it. */
.splash-stage
{
	position: relative;
	flex: none;
	width: var(--launcher-width);
	height: var(--launcher-height);
}

/* Fading out as the launcher appears. */
body.splash.gone
{
	opacity: 0;
}

.splash-slab,
.splash-pour
{
	position: absolute;
	left: var(--splash-slab-left);
	top: var(--splash-slab-top);
	width: var(--splash-slab-width);
	height: var(--splash-slab-height);
}

.splash-slab
{
	decorator: svg(brand/splash-slab.svg);
}

/* THE POUR: the gold name, clipped by a box that opens from the left while the program loads.
 * ITS WIDTH IS SET BY THE PROGRAM EVERY FRAME (ui_shell.cpp, poll_splash), measured along the name
 * from --splash-name-from to --splash-name-to: to --splash-pour-pause-at over --splash-pour-first, held for
 * --splash-pour-hold, then the rest over --splash-pour-rest, each on the easing token's curve. It was a transition on a
 * class, and RmlUi never animated it: the gold appeared whole the moment the class landed (the
 * user, 2026-10-13: "still not starting grey and filling"). */
/* CLIP ALWAYS (the user, 2026-10-13: "the splash still starts fully filled gold rather than
 * animating"). RmlUi clips an overflow: hidden box only when it counts content overflowing it, and
 * the gold name is absolutely placed, which it does not count, so the box never clipped and the
 * whole name showed at every width. clip: always makes it clip whatever it holds. */
.splash-pour
{
	overflow: hidden;
	clip: always;
	width: 0%;
}

.splash-gold
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: var(--splash-slab-width);
	height: var(--splash-slab-height);
	decorator: svg(brand/splash-gold.svg);
}

.splash-md
{
	position: absolute;
	left: var(--splash-emblem-left);
	top: var(--splash-emblem-top);
	width: var(--splash-emblem-width);
	height: var(--splash-emblem-height);
}

/* The mark in the disc, raised to sit optically centered (the user, 2026-10-12): 64 by 53.3 at
 * (68, 57.4) of the medallion's 200 by 190. */
.splash-md .splash-mark
{
	position: absolute;
	left: 34%;
	top: 30.21%;
	width: 32%;
	height: 28.05%;
}

.splash-foot
{
	position: absolute;
	left: var(--splash-foot-side);
	right: var(--splash-foot-side);
	bottom: var(--splash-foot-bottom);
	display: flex;
	justify-content: space-between;
	align-items: baseline;
}

.splash-by
{
	font-weight: var(--weight-body-strong);
	font-size: var(--size-note);
}

.splash-loading
{
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	font-family: var(--font-mono);
	font-size: var(--size-label);
	letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
	text-transform: uppercase;
}

.splash-pip
{
	width: var(--splash-pip);
	height: var(--splash-pip);
	margin-right: var(--space-3);
	background-color: var(--color-gold);
	animation: var(--splash-pip-pulse) var(--ease) infinite alternate pip;
}

@keyframes pip
{
	from { opacity: 0.25; }
	to { opacity: 1; }
}

/* The medallion moves as it does on the canvas, its rim gold (the logo's, not the focus's lime):
 * the fan breathes and the glint runs round the rim, with medallion.rcss's own keyframes. */
.splash-md .ly.leaf-l-o1, .splash-md .ly.leaf-l-o2 { animation: var(--fan-cycle) var(--ease) infinite fan-l; }
.splash-md .ly.leaf-l-i1, .splash-md .ly.leaf-l-i2 { animation: var(--fan-cycle) var(--fan-step) var(--ease) infinite fan-l; }
.splash-md .ly.leaf-l-c { animation: var(--fan-cycle) var(--fan-step-2) var(--ease) infinite fan-l; }
.splash-md .ly.leaf-r-o1, .splash-md .ly.leaf-r-o2 { animation: var(--fan-cycle) var(--ease) infinite fan-r; }
.splash-md .ly.leaf-r-i1, .splash-md .ly.leaf-r-i2 { animation: var(--fan-cycle) var(--fan-step) var(--ease) infinite fan-r; }
.splash-md .ly.leaf-r-c { animation: var(--fan-cycle) var(--fan-step-2) var(--ease) infinite fan-r; }
.splash-md .ly.glint { animation: var(--glint-cycle) var(--ease) infinite glint; }
<rml>
<head>
    <title>Splash</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="medallion.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="cut.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="splash.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- THE SPLASH (the menus plan, phase 99; the user, 2026-10-12: "Loading for a few seconds
     before the launher"), as decided on design-canvas://96729e1b, option D, Lockup: the medallion
     over the left end of a carved stone slab, the name filling with gold from the left while the
     program loads, "Developed by Jonathan Barnes" and the loading word along the foot. The slab
     and the gold are drawn layers (assets/ui/brand/, tools/brand_art.mjs); the medallion is the
     shipped Leaf fan with the mark's shader in its disc. Shown only before Play, in the
     launcher's window, for at least a few seconds; the shell takes over as it fades. -->
<body class="splash" id="splash">
    <div class="survey"></div>
    <!-- The launcher's own 960 by 620, centered in the window, which opens maximized
         (the user, 2026-10-13). -->
    <div class="splash-stage">
    <div class="splash-slab"></div>
    <div class="splash-pour" id="splash-pour"><div class="splash-gold"></div></div>
    <div class="md splash-md">
        <div class="ly shadows"></div>
        <div class="ly leaf-l-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-l-c"></div>
        <div class="ly leaf-r-o1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-o2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i1"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-i2"></div><div class="ly leaf-r-c"></div>
        <div class="ly rim"></div>
        <div class="ly glint"></div>
        <div class="mark splash-mark"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="splash-foot">
        <span class="splash-by">Developed by Jonathan Barnes</span>
        <span class="splash-loading"><span class="splash-pip"></span><span>Loading</span></span>
    </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
